Description: A 3D project's timeline preview writes its chunks with a DNxHD profile
 A 3D project's preview chunks hold both eyes, so the chunk consumer asks for
 twice the profile's width (patch 0023). DNxHD, the codec of Kdenlive's DNxHD
 preview profiles, takes a fixed list of frame sizes, none of them two eyes
 wide: FFmpeg's encoder refused the frame ("video parameters incompatible with
 DNxHD"), MLT's consumer then ended (melt: a segmentation fault), and no chunk
 was written, with nothing said. A DNxHD preview of a 3D project now names
 DNxHR HQ, the same codec's profile for any frame size (8 bits, 4:2:2, as the
 DNxHD profiles). Other preview profiles and 2D projects do not change.
Author: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Forwarded: not-yet
Last-Update: 2026-11-22
diff --git a/src/timeline2/view/previewmanager.cpp b/src/timeline2/view/previewmanager.cpp
index 710c06f..eb63438 100644
--- a/src/timeline2/view/previewmanager.cpp
+++ b/src/timeline2/view/previewmanager.cpp
@@ -713,6 +713,11 @@ void PreviewManager::doPreviewRender(const QString &scene)
         if (!sized) {
             consumerParams << QStringLiteral("width=%1").arg(m_stereoPair.width()) << QStringLiteral("height=%1").arg(m_stereoPair.height());
         }
+        // DNxHD (the DNxHD preview profiles) takes a fixed list of frame sizes, none of them two eyes wide: the encoder refuses the
+        // frame and no chunk is written. DNxHR, the same codec's profiles for any frame size, writes it
+        if (consumerParams.contains(QStringLiteral("vcodec=dnxhd")) && !consumerParams.join(QLatin1Char(' ')).contains(QLatin1String("vprofile="))) {
+            consumerParams << QStringLiteral("vprofile=dnxhr_hq");
+        }
     }
     QStringList args{QStringLiteral("preview-chunks"),
                      scene,
